    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 25 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule: **`SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`**.\n\nSince the tier is derived entirely from two already-stored fields (`namesakeCount` and `email`), I computed it at read time rather than adding a DB column or pipeline step:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, which generates the field (and setter) on the `OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` computed getter:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getMembershipTier() {\n       boolean unique = this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0;\n       boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n       return unique && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nMapStruct's `toOwnerDto` maps the getter to the new DTO field automatically, so both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response expose it with no extra wiring. The `@Transient` annotation keeps it out of persistence (it's derived, not stored).\n\nBoth new tests (`Cp15Tests`: SILVER for a unique owner with email, BRONZE for one without email) pass, and all 25 acceptance tests remain green.",
